{"id":56380,"ord":122,"n_segments":182,"prev":56379,"next":56381,"doc":{"id":"68113","title":"68113_Barney Bigard oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Albany Leon \"Barney\" Bigard","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68113/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68113"},"chapter":"Los Angeles and Kid Ory","title":"Downtown Los Angeles theaters: the Pantages and the Million Dollar","category":"venue_city_scene","summary":"They sort out the Orpheum and Pantages downtown theaters with stage-show bands, and Bigard worked one with Freddie Slack that later became the Million Dollar.","period":"1940s","year_from":1940,"year_to":1949,"words":145,"start":[138,12],"end":[139,17],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68113#s56380","tags":{"places":[{"name":"Los Angeles","focus":0,"type":"city"},{"name":"Hollywood","focus":0,"type":"neighborhood","in":"Los Angeles"}],"venues":[{"name":"Orpheum Theater","focus":1,"city":"Los Angeles"},{"name":"Pantages Theater","focus":1,"city":"Los Angeles"},{"name":"Million Dollar Theater","focus":1,"city":"Los Angeles"}],"bands":[{"name":"Freddie Slack's band","focus":0,"leader":"Freddie Slack"}]},"people":[{"name":"Freddie Slack","qid":"Q204969","n":1},{"name":"Pantages","qid":null,"n":1}],"story":{"theme":13,"theme_name":"Medicine shows, minstrels, circuses and the black theater circuit","community":23,"community_name":"On the road with minstrel, carnival and tent shows","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":138,"b":12,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Well, but there was music in the theaters, weren't there, downtown?"},{"p":138,"b":13,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"Yes."},{"p":138,"b":14,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Which ones?"},{"p":138,"b":15,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"Orpheum and the --"},{"p":138,"b":16,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Paramount?"},{"p":139,"b":0,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"Paramount or Pantages, one of them."},{"p":139,"b":1,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Pantages was the one from Hollywood."},{"p":139,"b":2,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"Hollywood."},{"p":139,"b":3,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Was there a Pantages downtown?"},{"p":139,"b":4,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"Yeah, there's two."},{"p":139,"b":5,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Did the Pantages in -- the Pantages in Hollywood had stage shows like Maglin Kiddies dancing but did they also have bands?"},{"p":139,"b":6,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"Oh, they had bands because we played there. I worked there with Freddie Slack, but now it turned into, like, a Mexican --"},{"p":139,"b":7,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Oh, that's the Million Dollars."},{"p":139,"b":8,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"Yeah, that changed to the Million Dollars, Theater."},{"p":139,"b":9,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Oh, the Million Dollar Theater was originally the Pantages?"},{"p":139,"b":10,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"Yeah, I think so."},{"p":139,"b":11,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"I didn't realize that."},{"p":139,"b":12,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"Yeah."},{"p":139,"b":13,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"Yeah, that's at Third and Broadway."},{"p":139,"b":14,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":139,"b":15,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"But they had stage shows. They had music right up into the early fifties, --"},{"p":139,"b":16,"s":"MR. BIGARD","x":"Oh, yeah."},{"p":139,"b":17,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"-- they had jazz bands."}]}